From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Kleinschmidt <kleinschmidtorama@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:51:05 -0400
Subject: [device] Notify DeviceMonitorWin observers before destruction

DeviceMonitorWin instances are owned by a process-wide message window
that an AtExitManager callback deletes. An observer that is still alive
at that point is left holding a dangling pointer to the monitor.

This happens to SerialDeviceEnumeratorWin::UiThreadHelper at browser
shutdown. DeviceService lives in the UI thread's SequenceLocalStorage,
so it is destroyed by BrowserTaskExecutor::Shutdown(), which runs after
BrowserMainLoop has shut down the ThreadPool. DeviceService holds the
SerialPortManagerImpl in a SequenceBound on a ThreadPool sequence, so
the task that would delete it (and the enumerator and helper it owns) is
dropped. The helper's ScopedObservation is still live when AtExitManager
deletes the monitor, which fails CheckDanglingRawPtrBufferEmpty() at
exit when dangling pointer checks are enabled.

Add DeviceMonitorWin::Observer::OnDeviceMonitorDestroying(), called from
~DeviceMonitorWin(), and have the serial helper reset its observation
there. HidServiceWin and UsbServiceWin are destroyed with DeviceService
on the UI thread, before AtExit, so they don't need it.

Bug: 572741653

Upstreamed at https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8561777.
This patch can be removed once that CL lands.

